        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: opéra comique\n- Places: Paris theatre of the same name\n- Works: Carmen, Aida, novella Carmen\n- People: Georges Bizet, Henri Meilhac, Ludovic Halévy, Prosper Mérimée, Giuseppe Verdi, Nell Rankin\n- Roles: Amneris, title role\n\nFacts:\n- Opéra comique is associated with a Paris theatre of the same name.\n- Opéra comique is not always comic or light in nature.\n- Carmen is perhaps the most famous opéra comique, and Carmen is a tragedy.\n- Carmen is an opera in four acts by French composer Georges Bizet.\n- Henri Meilhac and Ludovic Halévy wrote the libretto for Carmen.\n- Henri Meilhac and Ludovic Halévy based the libretto for Carmen on Prosper Mérimée's novella of the same title.\n- Nell Rankin was particularly admired for her portrayals of Amneris in Giuseppe Verdi's Aida and the title role in Georges Bizet's Carmen.",
